You will need to insert the "Debug.Assert" statements using appropriate C# syntax and logic that can parse the comments related to the variables to assert statements. Please note this is a basic and naive way to parse and generate assert statements. For complex conditional statements that cannot be parsed, you might need to develop a more sophisticated approach.--------------------
Debug.Assert(index >= 0);
</code>

Please note that your real requirements would greatly depend on the full scope of the comments you want to convert. This is just a simple example. 

Also, in C#, comments that start with "//" are single-line comments and those that start with "/*" and "*/" are multi-line comments. Debug.Assert statements are different and can only be used where C# code can be inserted. For example, in a method, in a loop, in a conditional statement, etc., and not in comments. When these are inside comments, they wouldn't be valid C# statements.

Remember the Debug class is part of the System.Diagnostics in C#, make sure you import it or put it at the top of your file.

```cs
using System.Diagnostics;
```--------------------